# Inventory item catalogue.

item crowbar "crowbar"
  look "A crowbar with ambitions well beyond leaning on bollards."

item mushroom "jet-caps"
  look "Jet-caps. Black-capped, wet, and worth more than they look. They grow in timber the fog has been at, and Marta will not serve her broth without them."

item licence_form "licence form"
  look "A blank Seafarer's Licence. Name, rank, and a box marked “previous piracy, if any”. Worthless until it carries the harbour stamp."

item drawer_key "drawer key"
  look "Bramwick's drawer key. Lost at cards, traded for a handful of mushrooms. A distinguished career, for a key."

item stamp "harbour stamp"
  look "The harbour stamp. Brass, heavy, and far more powerful than it looks."

item licence "stamped licence"
  look "My Seafarer's Licence, stamped by a clerk of the customs house in the Harbourmaster's legal absence. The ink is still wet."

item compass "brass compass"
  look "My father's compass. My grandfather made it, my father sailed by it, and then one morning he left it on the hall table and sailed without it. It has never once pointed north."
  state if act 1 and has licence and has manifest and ledger_read
    look "The needle points at the customs house like a dog that's found something. Bramwick, then. With everything."
  state if act 1 and has licence and not ledger_read
    look "The needle leans toward the lane. The harbour ledger is up in the loft over the chandler's."
  state if act 1 and has licence and not has manifest
    look "Bramwick wants the Arcadia's manifest copy. The chandler keeps one, if somebody settles his invoices."
  state if act 1 and has stamp and not has licence
    look "A harbour stamp and a clerk who knows where the licence forms are. Even the needle can see where this is going."
  state if act 1 and has drawer_key
    look "Bramwick's drawer key. The needle points at the customs house, or at least doesn't object to it."
  state if act 1 and has mushroom
    look "Someone in Port Vela wants what grows under the pier. The needle swings toward the tavern, and waits."
  state if act 1 and knows_key
    look "Marta has the drawer key and wants jet-caps. They come up under the stacked crate on the pier."
  state if act 1
    look "My father's compass. It has never once pointed north. Tonight it leans toward the customs house: Bramwick will know how a clerk gets a licence."
  state if act 2 and vane_convinced
    look "The needle has stopped pretending to be a compass. It points over the bow, into the fog, at a reef nobody sails. Forward, then."
  state if act 2 and quill_navigator and crew_agree
    look "A navigator, a crew, and Pell's last sentence in my pocket. The needle points aft, at the captain's cabin, and waits."
  state if act 2 and has sextant
    look "Pell's sextant. The needle swings toward the one person on board who wants to be a navigator more than she wants breakfast."
  state if act 2 and vane_terms and dinner and not chest_open
    look "Hobb has gone to his dinner. The needle points below decks, at a sea-chest nobody opens."
  state if act 2 and vane_terms and dinner and not crew_agree
    look "Hobb won't sail south for money, only for blood. I'm carrying a list of twenty-two names. The needle has opinions about that."
  state if act 2 and vane_terms and not dinner
    look "Three terms, and a bosun sitting on Pell's chest until dinner. The needle points below decks, toward a cook without a stamp."
  state if act 2 and quill_helped
    look "The needle wants the captain's cabin. Down the companionway at the stern, and onto her chart."
  state if act 2 and has spyglass
    look "Quill's spyglass. She wants it back, and I want to get past her. Commerce."
  state if act 2
    look "The needle points aft, past the lookout. Quill won't let a clerk by unless he's useful."
  state if act 3 and has flag16
    look "The needle points back across the flats at the wreck and her halyard, like a dog that wants to be let out. Sixteen, then. Up."
  state if act 3 and quill_free
    look "My father, in a salt pan, with a flag under his arm. For once the needle has nothing to add. Talk to him."
  state if act 3 and form9
    look "Form 9, written out clean and stamped. The needle points at Pike, who is going to love it. Then hate it. Then love it."
  state if act 3 and knows_form9
    look "There isn't a Form 9 on all of Gullet Key. There's a clerk with a harbour stamp and the blank back of a Bill of Health."
  state if act 3 and fog_down
    look "Quill is locked in the store hut, pending inspection. The needle points at Pike. Somebody here knows what form lets a person out."
  state if act 3 and gate_open and has bucket_water
    look "A bucket of lagoon, and a brazier making all the fog. The needle points at the Weather Works with a certain relish."
  state if act 3 and gate_open and has bucket
    look "The great brazier at the Weather Works is making the fog. My bucket is empty. The lagoon isn't."
  state if act 3 and gate_open
    look "The great brazier is making the fog, and fire hates water. There was a bucket in my father's cabin."
  state if act 3 and has bill and bill_smoked and bill_stamped and bill_signed and bill_dated
    look "Fumigated, stamped, countersigned and dated. The needle swings toward Pike, practically wagging."
  state if act 3 and has calendar_leaf
    look "A day, torn off Pike's calendar. The needle points at the Bill of Health, where days belong."
  state if act 3 and has bill and not bill_smoked
    look "The bill smells of cupboard. Pike's fumigation brazier smoulders right beside his gate."
  state if act 3 and has bill and not bill_stamped
    look "A Bill of Health without a harbour stamp. I happen to have a harbour stamp. The needle is embarrassed for me."
  state if act 3 and has bill and not bill_signed
    look "It wants a ship's officer's countersignature. The needle swings toward the only navigator on the island."
  state if act 3 and has bill and not bill_dated
    look "Undated. Pike's calendar is in his hut, and Pike can't take his eyes off it. Unless he's reciting something, eyes shut."
  state if act 3 and log_read
    look "Pike wants a Bill of Health. Every captain carries blanks; my father's are in the pigeonholes by his desk."
  state if act 3 and hatch_open
    look "The needle points down the hatch, at my father's desk. It's been waiting three years. So have I."
  state if act 3
    look "The needle points at the Arcadia's deck hatch, which is jammed. Quill packed a crowbar. Of course she did."
  state if act 4 and ledger_written
    look "The needle points down the pier, at a bollard with a navigator sitting on it. For once I don't need telling."
  state if act 4 and quarantine_lifted and not iou_paid
    look "The needle swings toward Bramwick, who keeps patting his coat pocket as if something in it might make a run for it."
  state if act 4 and quarantine_lifted
    look "A stamp, a ledger, and a page that's been wrong for three years. The needle points at the bar of the Salty Keel."
  state if act 4 and inquiry_done
    look "Bramwick is reinstated in everything but his stamp, which is in my pocket. The needle points at him, a little reproachfully."
  state if act 4 and has ledger and has purse and has claims_book and not kelp_proof
    look "Everything Bramwick asked for. The needle points at the Keel, where Cray is raising a glass. Then it twitches once toward the pier end, as if it's heard something about kelp."
  state if act 4 and has ledger and has purse and has claims_book
    look "The ledger, the purse, the claims book, my father's log and a manifest that smells of fog. The needle points at the Salty Keel, and Cray."
  state if act 4 and has requisition and req_stamped
    look "A stamped requisition. The needle points at Nib, who is going to enjoy not reading it."
  state if act 4 and has requisition
    look "A requisition without a stamp. The needle looks at the pocket where the stamp is, and then at me."
  state if act 4 and seen:nib.claims2 and not has claims_book
    look "Nib only answers to stamped requisitions, and there's a tray of blank ones on his desk."
  state if act 4 and seen:bramwick4.paper and not purse_given
    look "“A man who was there when it happened.” The needle swings toward the corner of the Keel, where Rook is pretending not to listen."
  state if act 4 and seen:bramwick4.paper and not ledger_taken
    look "The harbour ledger, chained to its desk in the loft. I have a crowbar. The needle has an opinion."
  state if act 4 and seen:bramwick4.paper and not has claims_book
    look "Cray's insurance books live at Cray & Co., up Chandler's Lane. The needle points that way with distaste."
  state if act 4 and farewell
    look "Cray has the chair, the ink and the dawn bell. The needle points at the Salty Keel, where a suspended harbourmaster is drinking."
  state if act 4
    look "The needle points out at the Marrow, at anchor past the boom. Quill is on the rail."

item spyglass "spyglass"
  look "A brass spyglass, dented twice and polished a thousand times. Somebody on this ship is squinting a lot this morning."

item sextant "Pell's sextant"
  look "Pell's sextant, polished to a mirror by forty years of thumbs. It measures the angle between a star and the sea, which is the kind of paperwork I can respect."

item pell_log "Pell's log"
  look "Pell's last entry: “If Ansel's boy ever comes aboard with the old man's compass, tell the captain she should”. Then nothing. Ansel's boy. That's me. I read it twice."
  state if seen:vane.pell
    look "Pell's last entry: “If Ansel's boy ever comes aboard with the old man's compass, tell the captain she should”. Then nothing. He died mid-sentence. Vane said so."

item bill "Bill of Health"
  look "A Bill of Health."
  state if form9
    look "Front: a Bill of Health, passed. Back: FORM 9, RELEASE OF DETAINED PERSONS, in my best hand. Both sides stamped. It's the best thing I've ever written."
  state if gate_open
    look "The Arcadia's Bill of Health: fumigated, stamped, countersigned, dated and inspected. Pike made me promise to keep it on my person. The back is still blank."
  state if bill_smoked and bill_stamped and bill_signed and bill_dated
    look "Fumigated, stamped, countersigned and dated. It's perfect. Pike is going to cry, and I may join him."
  state if not bill_smoked
    look "A Bill of Health for the Arcadia. It needs fumigating, a harbour stamp, a ship's officer's countersignature and a date. Right now it smells of cupboard."
  state if not bill_stamped
    look "A Bill of Health, smelling of kelp smoke. Still wants a harbour stamp, and whatever else it wants."
  state if not bill_signed
    look "Fumigated and stamped. The line marked SHIP'S OFFICER is empty, and so, possibly, is the date."
  state if not bill_dated
    look "Fumigated, stamped, and countersigned “QUILL, NAVIGATOR”. All it lacks is a date, which is what everybody forgets."

item calendar_leaf "calendar leaf"
  look "Today, torn off Pike's calendar. GULLET KEY QUARANTINE STATION. Underneath, in pencil, somebody has written: “Nothing happened.” Not today, it hasn't."

item bucket "bucket"
  look "A bailing bucket off the Arcadia. Empty. It's spent nine years keeping the sea out; it might enjoy carrying some in."

item bucket_water "bucket of lagoon"
  look "A bucket of lagoon, heavier than it looks, and it looks heavy. A small fish has come along for the ride. I'll put him back after."

item flag16 "flag sixteen"
  look "Flag number sixteen, made of shirts. One of the patches is a shirt I outgrew when I was twelve. In the corner, in red thread, an L."

item ansel_log "Ansel's log"
  look "My father's log. Six ships, fifteen flags, and one page that isn't to anyone on the sea at all. It's to my mother."

# Act IV
item purse "Rook's purse"
  look "A small leather purse sealed with a wax cloud. Rook's pay for leaving the Arcadia quietly. The seal has never been broken, which is the most honest thing about it."

item requisition "requisition"
  look "A blank Cray & Co. requisition. I've filled it in: one claims book, insurance, all of it. It wants a stamp. Without one it's just handwriting with ambitions."
  state if req_stamped
    look "REQUISITION: one claims book, insurance, all of it. Authorised: Harbour of Port Vela. Stamped. Nib won't read a word of it, which is the beauty of the thing."

item claims_book "claims book"
  look "Cray & Co.'s insurance claims. Six ships paid in full, for weather. On the facing page, the same year: Captain Vane's storm, refused on a technicality. Somebody underlined it, smugly."

item ledger "harbour ledger"
  look "The harbour ledger, with a length of broken chain still hanging off it. ARCADIA: lost at sea, three days before she was late. Paid, Cray & Co. The page is waiting for a correction."
  state if ledger_written
    look "ARCADIA: returned. All hands. In my hand, under Bramwick's, stamped. The best entry in the book."

item kelp_manifest "kelp manifest"
  look "QUARANTINE STN, G.K. Briquettes, kelp, four hundred. Purpose, in a careful clerk's hand: for fog. Someone at Cray & Co. writes down exactly what he's told."

item manifest "manifest copy"
  look "The Arcadia's manifest. Twenty-two names, every one marked lost, except one: “R. Rook, navigator. Discharged at sea.” Discharged by whom, in the middle of the sea?"
